# GROUND ABOVE THE GROUND (docs/ABOVE.md S1-S2): a slab of rock staged over the
# moss's heart with `--above=roof` (AboveStage), its west edge two tiles west
# of where the player starts. From above (law 3, docs/LOOK.md), the mass the
# player is under is architecture, cut at the section plane: under it, the roof
# is gone over the player and its outline is chalked, dashed, on the ground in
# its shade; out from under it, it is whole again. Over the shoulder the cut
# stands down and the roof is a ceiling: the underside overhead, then its rim
# from outside.
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/above-roof.tour --seed=1 --place=moss --above=roof --hour=10.5 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
wait 0.6
await above_cut 3
shot 01-under-the-roof-from-above-cut
walk -1,-0.45 1.6
await above_whole 3
shot 02-out-from-under-it-whole
walk 1,0.45 1.6
await above_cut 3
shot 03-back-under-cut-again
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
await above_whole 3
wait 0.8
shot 04-under-the-roof-a-ceiling with shoulder
mouse 0,-260 0.4
wait 0.8
shot 05-up-at-the-underside with shoulder
mouse 0,260 0.4
leap 1.5
wait 0.6
shot 06-out-past-its-edge with shoulder
mouse 1100,0 0.8
wait 0.8
shot 07-back-at-the-rim with shoulder
